Between $x=0$ and $x=2$ the cubic $y=x^3$ lies above the quadratic (for example at $x=1$: $1>-3$), so
$$\begin{aligned} A&=\int_0^2\left(x^3-(7x^2-10x)\right)dx \\ &=\left[\dfrac{x^4}{4}-\dfrac{7x^3}{3}+5x^2\right]_0^2 \\ &=\dfrac{2^4}{4}-\dfrac{7(2)^3}{3}+5(2)^2-0 \\ &=4-\dfrac{56}{3}+20 \\ &=\dfrac{16}{3} \\ &=5\dfrac{1}{3}\text{ units}^2 \end{aligned}$$

